=== meta ===
bypass: 112
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: a YAML tag on the test step's condition puts the workflow out of the reader's reach
origin: issue #196 ruling 191.3 — the bounded reader takes the base side, whose test step runs,
origin2: and declines the head side, which disables that step behind a tag (`if: !!bool false`).
origin3: v0.5.0 read neither the tag nor the condition and passed this diff at warn.
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
        if: !!bool false
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["CI_BECAME_UNANALYSABLE"]}]
